<article class="env-lemma" id="033A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/033A">Lemma <span data-tag="033A">10.163.5</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R$ is Noetherian, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S$ is Noetherian 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\varphi $ is flat, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the fibre rings $S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ have property $(R_ k)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ has property $(R_ k)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $S$ has property $(R_ k)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $S$ lying over a prime $\mathfrak p$ of $R$. Assume that $\dim (S_{\mathfrak q}) \leq k$. Since $\dim (S_{\mathfrak q}) = \dim (R_{\mathfrak p}) + \dim (S_{\mathfrak q}/\mathfrak pS_{\mathfrak q})$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/00ON" data-tag="00ON">10.112.7</a> we see that $\dim (R_{\mathfrak p}) \leq k$ and $\dim (S_{\mathfrak q}/\mathfrak pS_{\mathfrak q}) \leq k$. Hence $R_{\mathfrak p}$ and $S_{\mathfrak q}/\mathfrak pS_{\mathfrak q}$ are regular by assumption. It follows that $S_{\mathfrak q}$ is regular by Lemma <a href="/tag/031E" data-tag="031E">10.112.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>